# Training inputs and intermediates. The corpora are large and re-downloadable;
# only wake/models/ ships. See README.md for the pipeline, data/README.md for
# what lives in data/.
#
# data/* rather than data/ so the negations below work: git does not descend
# into an ignored directory, so a negation under `data/` would never match.
data/*
!data/README.md

# Recordings used to be committed here — they cannot be regenerated, so
# keeping them in git was the backup. They moved to ~/.config/neon/wake/ on
# 2026-08-03, when this repo went public: my_voice/ is 103 recordings of a
# real person's voice, which is not something to publish as a side effect of
# open-sourcing a kitchen assistant. run.sh mounts them back into the
# container at the old paths, so nothing in the pipeline changed.
#
# They are no longer backed up by committing them. See data/README.md.

output/
logs/
__pycache__/
